@*
    Feature switching. This used to be an empty file with a comment saying the home page
    "lists and describes every function" — true, but it meant the only route out of a
    feature was the brand logo, and moving from Rap Roast to Meme cost a trip through
    home and past six model pickers. ActiveImageBar still carried a comment calling this
    "the single source of truth" for feature switching, which had quietly become false.

    The active image survives navigation, so switching here is genuinely cheap: you keep
    your photo and change what happens to it. That is the board's own idea — one photo,
    many destinations — so the rail names the destinations.
*@
<nav class="app-nav__links" aria-label="Features">
    @foreach (var (href, label) in Features)
    {
        <NavLink class="app-nav__link" href="@href" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">@label</NavLink>
    }
</nav>

@code {
    // Order matches the Studio board's rows, so the rail and the home page cannot disagree
    // about what this app does or what order it does it in.
    private static readonly (string Href, string Label)[] Features =
    [
        ("/image-regeneration", "Regenerate"),
        ("/meme-generation",    "Meme"),
        ("/bulk-generate",      "Bulk"),
        ("/rap-roast",          "Roast"),
        ("/style-director",     "Style"),
        ("/gallery",            "Gallery"),
    ];
}
